⚠ COPYLEFT WARNING FOR CONTRIBUTORS
    reference/gringer/path_extrude.scad (GPLv3) is a working polyhedron-based
    sweep engine, and is therefore the single most tempting file to copy from
    while writing src/ut_mesh.scad. DO NOT. `just lint` blocks `use <>` from
    reference/, but it cannot detect copy-paste. Read for understanding; write
    from the geometry. The same applies to reference/doommeister/.

    reference/axford/libs/vector.scad is GPL and was `use <>`d by every core
    file in the pre-2026 layout. OpenSCAD's `use <>` is source-level inclusion
    at parse time. Nothing in src/ may reference it. Its six consumed functions
    (mod, cross, dot, unitv, anglev, orientate) are OpenSCAD builtins or
    one-liners today; src/ut_math.scad reimplements them from the definitions.
